sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/holdout-clade-aves-blind-for-all-current-tests> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The public tables cannot support a blind clade exam at the builders' own minimum n: with Aves held out 13 birds against 50 for kimura-heterozygosity, 8 birds against 15 for hamilton-senescence; Aves was confirmed on 2026-10-31 knowing this, over a Mammalia holdout that would make 1 of 2 exams decisive but 3 already-built tests post hoc" ;
    dct:description "Status: established by enumeration of the project's own files (not a scientific hypothesis). The finding first: for the laws tested so far, the public trait and demographic tables leave too few held-out bird species to meet the builders' own pre-registered minimum sample sizes (kimura-heterozygosity: 13 against 50; hamilton-senescence: 8 against 15), so a blind clade exam at those minimums cannot yet decide. This is a result about the state of the data, not about the thread, and it is more useful to the next team than a decisive-looking number from a compromised design. The decision: class Aves was confirmed on 2026-10-31 by Amit Shenoy, project lead, in his own words to the hub: \"Sure do AVes\", relayed by the hub, after being provisional from the first freeze at 2026-10-31T05:52:44.982Z; the re-freeze left the roster unchanged. The cost was taken knowingly: Aves was chosen knowing it is underpowered for the tests built so far: the held-out bird counts fall below the builders’ own pre-registered minimum sample sizes, so both examined tests read inconclusive. Mammalia would have made 1 of 2 examined tests decisive, but the examined tests had already fitted on mammal rows, and one further completed test uses mammals only and would have been built entirely on held-out data; a switch now would have made those tests post hoc. The choice was therefore a clean blind that cannot yet decide over a decisive-looking test on a contaminated design, and the clean blind was taken. Of the 16 completed claim tests, 2 were examined on held-out birds and 14 contain no bird rows at all, so under the Aves holdout no completed test has fitted on held-out data. Under a Mammalia holdout, the 2 examined tests (which fitted on mammal rows) and thompson1917-ch16-13 (mammals only) would already be built on held-out data: 3 post hoc tests. Power: with the builders' own minimum sample sizes, Aves reaches a verdict in 0 of 2 examined tests and Mammalia in 1 of 2. Aves is the frozen and confirmed clade. It does not establish which clade is scientifically better; it establishes the blindness and power trade-off for the tests that exist today, and it will change as tests are added. Scope of the exam: it checks a builder's prediction on species the builder never saw, under the builder's own pre-registered rule and unit of analysis; it does not detect that a verdict depends on the operationalisation chosen. The hub's cross-check against the collaborator swarm (dashboard/public/crosscheck.json, 2026-10-31T14:13:42.226Z) shows that hazard is real: of 8 claims both swarms tested independently, 6 verdicts agree and 2 differ (darwin1859-ch11-13: ours supports, theirs mixed; thompson1917-ch03-07: ours supports, theirs mixed), each difference one of degree between supports and mixed under different operationalisations rather than a factual contradiction. Blindness to the clade and robustness to the operationalisation are two separate checks, and a claim needs both." ;
    delphi:context "Inventory sizes from holdout/split.json and holdout/alt/Mammalia/split.json: Aves 48 roster species (35 genome-ready at chromosome or complete level), Mammalia 43 roster species (31 genome-ready). Triage file: holdout/exam-results/not-applicable.json. Power file: holdout/power-analysis.json (2026-10-31T14:41:43.541Z)." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-holdout-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Power analysis: held-out n and the builders' minimum n for each examined test under Aves and Mammalia" ;
    dct:description "Each completed claim test’s analysis.py was copied to a scratch directory, its class filter (\"Aves\") swapped for the candidate clade, and run with --exam. The builder’s decision rule, including its minimum n, was then applied to the held-out species alone (holdout/exam-results/rules.mjs). The frozen Aves split was not changed." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Each completed claim test re-run with --exam on a scratch copy with the class filter swapped; the builder's own decision rule including its minimum n applied to the held-out species alone" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphibio.org/t/holdout/POWER.md> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:frozen-split ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphibio.org/t/holdout/data.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:status .
  sub:status a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "status" ;
    schema:value "established by enumeration of project files" ;
    schema:description "Status of this evidence item in the words of holdout/EXAM.md and AGENTS.md A10" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m1 .
  sub:m1 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_completed_claim_tests" ;
    schema:value "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "completed claim tests under claim-tests/ at build time" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m2 .
  sub:m2 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_tests_examined_on_aves" ;
    schema:value "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "tests whose data contain bird rows and that were examined on the frozen roster" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m3 .
  sub:m3 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_tests_without_bird_rows" ;
    schema:value "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "completed tests with no bird rows, logged as not applicable" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m4 .
  sub:m4 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_tests_post_hoc_if_mammalia" ;
    schema:value "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "already-built tests that fitted on mammal rows and would be post hoc under a Mammalia holdout" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m5 .
  sub:m5 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_decisive_exams_aves" ;
    schema:value "0"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "examined tests reaching a verdict with Aves held out" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m6 .
  sub:m6 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_decisive_exams_mammalia" ;
    schema:value "1"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "examined tests that would reach a verdict with Mammalia held out" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m7 .
  sub:m7 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_roster_species_aves" ;
    schema:value "48"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "held-out species on the Aves roster" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m8 .
  sub:m8 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_roster_species_mammalia" ;
    schema:value "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "species that a Mammalia roster would hold" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m9 .
  sub:m9 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_claims_cross_checked_with_collaborator_swarm" ;
    schema:value "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "claims tested independently by both this tree and the collaborator swarm (dashboard/public/crosscheck.json)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m10 .
  sub:m10 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_cross_check_agreements" ;
    schema:value "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "of those, verdicts that agree" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m11 .
  sub:m11 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "n_cross_check_disagreements" ;
    schema:value "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "of those, verdicts that differ under different operationalisations (supports against mixed), the hazard the held-out exam does not test" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m12 .
  sub:m12 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "held_out_n_kimura_heterozygosity_aves" ;
    schema:value "13"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "kimura-heterozygosity: held-out species with Aves held out (builder minimum 50; inconclusive)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m13 .
  sub:m13 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "held_out_n_kimura_heterozygosity_mammalia" ;
    schema:value "40"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "kimura-heterozygosity: held-out species with Mammalia held out (builder minimum 50; inconclusive)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m14 .
  sub:m14 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "held_out_n_hamilton_senescence_aves" ;
    schema:value "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "hamilton-senescence: held-out species with Aves held out (builder minimum 15; inconclusive)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/holdout-clade-power-analysis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m15 .
  sub:m15 a schema:PropertyValue ;
    schema:propertyID "held_out_n_hamilton_senescence_mammalia" ;
    schema:value "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    schema:description "hamilton-senescence: held-out species with Mammalia held out (builder minimum 15; mixed)" .
  sub:frozen-exam a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "holdout/exam.json (frozen roster and rules of the held-out exam; clade confirmed 2026-10-31; roster first frozen 2026-10-31T05:52:44Z)" ;
